From 709fc85ea20d630684f4e7bf7c613b2fe126553b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:02:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): mixed-skill marker remedy gives the
 device remedy; document auto_overridable_skill_markers

A card with skills [myapp-*, computer-use] and no placement hit the context
skill first, so its remedy said re-create with placement='auto' -- which still
pinned it local on computer-use. marker_remedy now re-checks the card as 'auto'
would see it and gives the device remedy right away.

Docs: kanban.placement.auto_overridable_skill_markers (default ^myapp, ^bb-)
in configuration.md and the config_defaults comment. check_docs_drift now also
checks open-dict sections (kanban.placement keys read via self.raw.get); the 4
pre-existing undocumented placement keys are baselined.

Follow-up to #1441 review (t_01a1cff2870061da); card t_01a1d005373dd9e8.
