-`kanban.placement` (default `{}`: every card is created locally) lets a gateway send cards that have no local-only need to another gateway. `kanban_create` creates such a card on the `route` target via `hermes-hub create-task` and binds it to the chat that asked for it. A card stays local when the caller passes `placement="local"`, when it uses options a remote create can't carry (parents, a project, a `dir`/`worktree` workspace, an initial status, a human request, a tenant; with a hermes-hub client older than 1.8.0, which lacks `create-task --option`, also a model pin, goal mode, triage or a non-local completion contract), when it needs a capability only this gateway holds, when its text matches a local marker (`local_markers` replaces the built-in list, `extra_local_markers` extends it; a bare MacBook or mini mention pins only from the title, not from a body verification step), or when the target isn't live. A text-marker local decision is reported on the `kanban_create` result as `placement` plus a one-line remedy. Other keys: `creator_session`, `local_skill_markers`, `assignees`, `hub_live_seconds`, `wait_seconds`, `hub_cli`.
+`kanban.placement` (default `{}`: every card is created locally) lets a gateway send cards that have no local-only need to another gateway. `kanban_create` creates such a card on the `route` target via `hermes-hub create-task` and binds it to the chat that asked for it. A card stays local when the caller passes `placement="local"`, when it uses options a remote create can't carry (parents, a project, a `dir`/`worktree` workspace, an initial status, a human request, a tenant; with a hermes-hub client older than 1.8.0, which lacks `create-task --option`, also a model pin, goal mode, triage or a non-local completion contract), when it needs a capability only this gateway holds, when its text matches a local marker (`kanban.placement.local_markers` replaces the built-in list, `kanban.placement.extra_local_markers` extends it; a bare MacBook or mini mention pins only from the title, not from a body verification step), or when the target isn't live. A text-marker local decision is reported on the `kanban_create` result as `placement` plus a one-line remedy. Other keys: `kanban.placement.creator_session`, `kanban.placement.local_skill_markers` (regexes on a card's skills that keep it local), `kanban.placement.auto_overridable_skill_markers`, `kanban.placement.assignees`, `kanban.placement.hub_live_seconds`, `wait_seconds`, `kanban.placement.hub_cli`.
+
+`kanban.placement.auto_overridable_skill_markers` (default `["^myapp", "^bb-"]`) lists the skill regexes that only say what a card is about, such as a Baby Bear repo skill on a Python fix. A card created with an explicit `placement="auto"` skips these skills in the local-marker scan, so it can run elsewhere. Device skills (`apple-*`, `macos-*`, `computer-use`, `ios-*`, a local Chrome) still keep it local, and an omitted placement honours every skill. A list replaces the default. The remedy on a skill-marker result names `placement="auto"` only when that would move the card: one that also carries a device skill is told to drop that skill instead.
